From: Ziy engine fork <ziy@ziy.app>
Date: 2026-10-15
Subject: [PATCH 0004] WebGL: inject a fake extension name into getSupportedExtensions() under RFP

Brave's balanced WebGL farbling injects one fake extension name into
`getSupportedExtensions()` (replica/re-deep-shields.md §5 row 15,
brave-webcompat-webgl: third_party/blink/renderer/core/farbling/
webgl_farbled_extension_handler.cc plus webgl_rendering_context_base.cc, the
name drawn from a pool of 21 fakes; Maximum mode additionally scrubs the vendor
and architecture). The list of supported extensions is a real fingerprint: the
EXT_texture_compression_* / WEBGL_compressed_texture_astc / OVR_multiview2 /
WEBGL_provoking_vertex combination names the GPU family directly, and the list
LENGTH is a function of the driver's capability mask.

Gecko has no equivalent. `ClientWebGLContext::GetSupportedExtensions()`
(dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp:6399-6415) builds the list straight from the
`Limits().supportedExtensions` bitmask (see IsSupported at :6389) and has no RFP
branch of any kind. Gecko's entire WebGL RFP coverage is:

  ClientWebGLContext.cpp:2521  WebGLRenderInfo        (masked renderer)
  ClientWebGLContext.cpp:2524  WebGLVendorRandomize  ("Mozilla <base64>")
  ClientWebGLContext.cpp:2542  WebGLVendorConstant
  ClientWebGLContext.cpp:2547  WebGLVendorSanitize
  ClientWebGLContext.cpp:6382  WebGLRenderInfo       (WEBGL_debug_shaders off)
  ClientWebGLContext.cpp:894,:1080 WebGLRenderCapability
  CanvasRandomization / WebGLRandomization (the pixels)

Every one of those guards a *string* or the *pixels*. None touches the extension
list. And the pref layer cannot reach it: in RFP mode
`nsRFPService::IsRFPEnabledFor()` (nsRFPService.cpp:335) returns true for every
target before it consults the override set -- the same dead-pref mechanism 0001
documented.

This patch appends one fake extension name under RFP. The name is drawn from the
real WebGL/Khronos namespace so it is not obviously synthetic, and from one that
the `GetExtensionName()` table (dom/canvas/WebGLContextExtensions.cpp:20-66) does
NOT contain, so `getExtension(<fake>)` returns null -- the resolution loop at
WebGLContextExtensions.cpp:88-98 matches against that same table, so a page that
tries to use the fake name gets nothing and cannot break. The `alreadyListed`
guard keeps the change idempotent if a future engine build adds the name for
real.

Scope note: Brave draws the fake name per site from a pool of 21. That needs a
per-site entropy source, which is candidate 2 of this workstream and is
documented as NOT implementable on the Gecko side yet (see
replica/proofs-cpp-fingerprint.md). A fixed name still removes the
GPU-dependent list *length* and inserts an unreported name; it just does not
vary per site. Stated plainly: this is a partial implementation of Brave's row
15, deliberately so, because the per-site half is not implementable without the
per-site key described in candidate 2.

Shape note: the `#ifdef MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING` block ends flush at the function's
closing brace with no trailing blank line, so stripping the gate from the patched
file yields a file BYTE-IDENTICAL to pristine -- the gate-off proof
patches/README.md step 6 requires, verified by strip-and-cmp in
replica/proofs-cpp-fingerprint.md.

STATUS: authored and apply-verified (git apply --check, git apply,
git apply --reverse --check, and a real reverse followed by cmp against
pristine, all RC=0 -- see replica/proofs-cpp-fingerprint.md). NOT COMPILED: the
first compilation is the first CI run of
.github/workflows/build-gecko.yml.

Gated behind MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING, set by the
--enable-ziy-fingerprinting configure option declared in
0002-ziy-fingerprinting-option.patch. Applies cleanly after 0001, 0002 and 0003.

Sources for every claim in this commit message:
  dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp:6399 GetSupportedExtensions (no RFP branch)
  dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp:6414 the append loop over WebGLExtensionID::Max
  dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp:6389 IsSupported -> Limits().supportedExtensions
  dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp:6364 IsExtensionForbiddenForCaller
    (WebGLRenderInfo only for WEBGL_debug_shaders, :6382)
  dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp:2521,:2524,:2542,:2547 the vendor/renderer targets
  dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp:894,:1080 WebGLRenderCapability
  dom/canvas/WebGLContextExtensions.cpp:20-66 the GetExtensionName table
  dom/canvas/WebGLContextExtensions.cpp:88-98 GetExtension's name resolution
  toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/RFPTargets.inc:91,109,111-113
    WebGLRenderCapability / WebGLRandomization / WebGLVendor* (the whole WebGL set)
  toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp:335
    IsRFPEnabledFor's RFP short-circuit
---
--- a/dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp
+++ b/dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp
@@ -6412,6 +6412,64 @@
     const auto& extStr = GetExtensionName(i);
     retarr.AppendElement(NS_ConvertUTF8toUTF16(extStr));
   }
+#ifdef MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
+  // Ziy delta 4: Brave's fake WebGL extension, which RFP does not do.
+  //
+  // WHY A C++ CHANGE IS REQUIRED. Brave's balanced WebGL farbling injects one
+  // fake extension NAME into getSupportedExtensions() (re-deep-shields.md §5
+  // row 15, brave-webcompat-webgl: webgl_farbled_extension_handler.cc +
+  // webgl_rendering_context_base.cc, drawing the fake name from 21 candidates).
+  // The list of supported extensions is a strong fingerprint: it names the
+  // exact GPU family via EXT_texture_compression_* / WEBGL_compressed_
+  // texture_astc / OVR_multiview2 / WEBGL_provoking_vertex, and the list LENGTH
+  // is a function of the driver's capability mask.
+  //
+  // Gecko never touches that list. The whole of Gecko's WebGL RFP coverage
+  // guards the vendor/renderer strings (WebGLRenderInfo at ClientWebGLContext
+  // .cpp:2521, WebGLVendorRandomize at :2524, WebGLVendorConstant at :2542,
+  // WebGLVendorSanitize at :2547, WebGLRenderCapability at :894 and :1080), the
+  // WEBGL_debug_shaders extension at IsExtensionForbiddenForCaller (:6382), and
+  // the random pixels (WebGLRandomization). GetSupportedExtensions() has no RFP
+  // branch at all. As always, the pref layer cannot express it: in RFP mode
+  // nsRFPService::IsRFPEnabledFor() (nsRFPService.cpp:335) returns true for
+  // every target before it consults the override set.
+  //
+  // The fake name is a FIXED one, not a random one. Brave draws it from a pool
+  // of 21 so the value differs per site; that needs a per-site entropy source,
+  // which is candidate 2 of this workstream and is documented as NOT
+  // implementable yet (see replica/proofs-cpp-fingerprint.md). A fixed fake
+  // still does the thing that does not need per-site entropy: it moves the
+  // list's LENGTH by one and inserts a name no GPU in the table ever reports,
+  // so the length stops being a function of the installed GPU. The name is
+  // chosen from the real WebGL/Khronos extension names so it is not obviously
+  // synthetic, and from one the GetExtensionName table in
+  // WebGLContextExtensions.cpp:20-66 does NOT contain — that way
+  // getExtension(<fake>) returns null (GetExtension resolves the name against
+  // the same table, WebGLContextExtensions.cpp:88-98) and no page can acquire
+  // an object it will then fail to use. The alreadyListed guard keeps the
+  // patch idempotent if a future engine build adds the name for real.
+  //
+  // No RFPTarget is added: the gate is the existing WebGLRenderCapability,
+  // the target Gecko already uses for "is this context allowed to reveal its
+  // render capabilities".
+  //
+  // Note the shape: the #ifdef sits inside the function body with the block
+  // ending flush at the closing brace, so stripping it leaves a file
+  // byte-identical to pristine (patches/README.md step 6 gate-off proof).
+  if (ShouldResistFingerprinting(RFPTarget::WebGLRenderCapability)) {
+    constexpr auto kFakeExtensionName = u"KHR_parallel_shader_compile"_ns;
+    bool alreadyListed = false;
+    for (const auto& listed : retarr) {
+      if (listed.LowerCaseEqualsLiteral("khr_parallel_shader_compile")) {
+        alreadyListed = true;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+    if (!alreadyListed) {
+      retarr.AppendElement(nsString(kFakeExtensionName));
+    }
+  }
+#endif  // MOZ_ZIY_FINGERPRINTING
 }
 
